<p>Peter Magyar, a former ally of Viktor Orban, is preparing to take office as Hungary’s next prime minister after his Tisza party defeated Orban’s Fidesz in Sunday’s election, ending Orban’s 16 years in power. In the first major post-election moves, Magyar said a new government could be in place by mid-May, called on Hungary’s president to resign, and promised to overhaul state media. The result is drawing broad attention across Europe because it could reshape Hungary’s ties with the European Union and NATO after years of friction under Orban, even as questions remain about how far policy will really shift on issues such as Ukraine, energy, and national sovereignty. Several outlets note that Magyar built support from both left- and right-leaning voters, giving Hungary an opening for political renewal while leaving his incoming government to balance very different expectations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/o0bwwB5mIchg0uEbGFUwjGELXw3dBrF-Z3LWlIstr1yKG5V9_5A_fPDPMGBpnzDXyvckjlEeWZfYKt1nH83ZIKwCfTdJKTuvy4HqqEBW3-7ROEN-NdBZB07jytJ3tq_9iBvKXfxweq1cZafhmVN25FR_-LnYvACk1nFfP4Ixi0vTTDxRQfUX5SOW4XeDew0k77jvnTQ0IzUtJT9lE6aw0Q' alt='Peter Magyar campaigning in 2024 in Viktor Orban’s hometown, Felcsut, Hungary.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Presidential rationale: In calling on the president to step down, Magyar said he was unworthy of embodying national unity and incapable of ensuring respect for the law.</li><li>Populism limits: Many read the result as a test of whether long-running right-wing populist rule has electoral limits in Hungary and beyond.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Peter Magyar/The Hindu: Magyar said the president was unworthy of embodying national unity and incapable of ensuring respect for the law, framing his resignation demand as part of restoring constitutional credibility. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/new-hungarian-leader-magyar-says-pro-orban-president-must-go/article70866123.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: Le Monde said Magyar rode a broad anti-Orban wave but now must turn that coalition into a governing program and clarify his position on Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/04/16/the-pitfalls-of-hungary-s-post-orban-transition_6752479_23.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>RT analysis: RT noted that some European commentary cast Putin as the biggest loser and Kyiv as a winner, but argued that Magyar may soften Hungary’s rhetoric more than abandon its core interests. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638466-orbans-exit-through-global-eyes/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Spiked commentary: Spiked argued that progressives should not assume Magyar’s win represents a leftward turn, portraying him instead as a different kind of right-leaning challenger to Orban. (<a href='https://www.spiked-online.com/2026/04/15/peter-magyars-victory-is-nothing-for-progressives-to-cheer/'>Spiked</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/14/world/europe/viktor-orban-peter-magyar-election.html'>How Peter Magyar Defeated Viktor Orban, a Former Ally, In Hungary’s Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638466-orbans-exit-through-global-eyes/'>Orban’s exit through global eyes: Who really gains – and who doesn’t</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.spiked-online.com/2026/04/15/peter-magyars-victory-is-nothing-for-progressives-to-cheer/'>Péter Magyar’s victory is nothing for ‘progressives’ to cheer</a> - spiked-online.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/04/16/the-pitfalls-of-hungary-s-post-orban-transition_6752479_23.html'>The pitfalls of Hungary&#x27;s post-Orban transition</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/hungarys-magyar-urges-president-to-quit-vows-to-overhaul-state-media'>Hungary’s Magyar urges president to quit, vows to overhaul state media</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/badenoch-orbans-defeat-gives-me-hope-for-the-center-right/'>Badenoch: Orbán’s defeat gives me hope for center right</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/what-changed-in-hungarys-election-explained/article70865139.ece'>What changed in Hungary’s election? | Explained</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>